plicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIPPON SHOOTER LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI SHIZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIRIYAMA SHIGERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOGA BUNICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUROSAWA KANJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI, SHIZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIRIYAMA, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGA, BUNICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUROSAWA, KANJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A transfer system comprising a traveling rail (1) forming a transfer route and a transfer body (3) capable of traveling on a traveling rail along the longitudinal direction of the traveling rail, wherein flexible drive tubes (5) are disposed on the traveling rail along the longitudinal direction of the traveling rail, the transfer body comprises traveling wheels (4) capable of rolling on the traveling rail and drive wheels (2) which receive a rotating drive force from the pressure of a pressure medium supplied to the drive tubes so as to be able to roll on the drive tubes while pressing these tubes, the traveling rail has a plurality of transfer sections and the transfer body can receive a rotating drive force from the drive tubes for each transfer section, and a transfer route change-over switch can be installed between the transfer sections so as to switch the transfer route as necessary.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un système de transfert comportant un rail de roulement (1) constituant un chemin de transfert et un corps de transfert (3) susceptible de se déplacer sur le rail de roulement longitudinalement audit rail. Dans ce système, des tubes d'entraînement souples (5) sont disposés sur le rail de roulement suivant la direction longitudinale dudit rail et le corps de transfert comporte des molettes (4) conçues pour rouler sur le rail de roulement et des molettes d'entraînement (2) qui reçoivent une force d'entraînement en rotation par l'intermédiaire de la pression exercée par un milieu de pression alimentant les tubes d'entraînement et qui peuvent ainsi rouler sur les tubes d'entraînement tout en comprimant ces tubes. Le rail de roulement comporte plusieurs sections de transfert et le corps de transfert peut recevoir une force d'entraînement en rotation appliquée par les tubes d'entraînement associés à chaque section de transfert, et un commutateur de changement de direction de transfert peut être installé entre les sections de transfert de façon à changer la direction de transfert si nécessaire.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the